messages:
alex_support: forwarding a customer issue — they see repeated aborted requests when the SDK retries against our API. they say it started after upgrading undici on their app. sample error: `FetchError: request aborted`

alex_support: paste from customer: 
```ts
// simplified client code
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ retries: 2, timeout: 200 }); // timeout in ms
// they call in a loop
await client.generate({ prompt });
```

alex_support: customer details: node v18.17.1, undici@5.14.0, @redwood/sdk v0.9.2. Occurs intermittently but reliably under burst load.

maria_eng: thanks — my first guess: undici/Node fetch semantics changed across versions re: AbortSignal propagation across retries. do they reuse the same AbortController for each attempt?

alex_support: customer says SDK handles timeouts internally and they didn't pass a signal. but their stack shows the same abort stack trace across retry attempts.

tom_runtime: can you ask for `npm ls undici` and a minimal repro? also need raw request/response traces from the SDK (enable DEBUG=redwood:sdk).

alex_support: requested traces, they attached this snippet from debug: 
```
[169XXXXX] attempt=0 send request
[169XXXXX] request aborted: FetchError: aborted
[169XXXXY] attempt=1 retry -> sending request
[169XXXXY] request aborted: FetchError: aborted
```

maria_eng: that pattern matches a bug where the SDK reused the original AbortSignal for retries. If the runtime triggers an abort (timeout), the same signal stays aborted and subsequent attempts fail instantly. undici 5.x sometimes surfaces this more due to internal optimizations.

sophie_sre: so two paths: short-term workaround -> ensure a fresh AbortController per attempt; long-term -> patch SDK to create per-attempt merged signal (timeout + user signal) and ensure we don't reuse a permanently-aborted signal.

maria_eng: suggested patch (pseudo): 
```ts
// inside sdk retry loop
for (let attempt=0; attempt<=maxRetries; attempt++) {
  const attemptController = new AbortController();
  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => attemptController.abort(), timeoutMs);
  // merge with user signal if provided
  const signal = mergeSignals(userSignal, attemptController.signal);
  try {
    await fetch(url, { signal });
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(timeoutId);
  }
}
```

maria_eng: mergeSignals = subscribe to both signals and abort combined controller when either fires. ensures each attempt gets a fresh non-aborted controller.

tom_runtime: agree. also add a guard: if userSignal is already aborted before retry loop, bail early. and add unit test to simulate abort-on-first-attempt.

alex_support: customer asked for a quick workaround they can apply now without waiting for an SDK release. suggestions?

sophie_sre: short-term: disable SDK auto-retries: set retries=0, and implement manual retry with fresh controller per attempt in app code. example: 
```ts
async function safeCall(client, payload) {
  for (let i=0;i<3;i++) {
    const c = new AbortController();
    const t = setTimeout(()=>c.abort(), 200);
    try {
      return await client.generate({ ...payload, signal: c.signal });
    } catch (e) {
      if (i===2) throw e;
      await sleep(50 * Math.pow(2,i)); // simple backoff with jitter
    } finally { clearTimeout(t); }
  }
}
```

maria_eng: additionally, ask them to `npm i undici@5.18.6` or upgrade Node to 20.x if feasible; some undici v5 patches changed behavior around signal lifecycle. but main fix is per-attempt controller.

tom_runtime: i'll open a bug PR to the SDK repo and target a canary build for dev later today. will include tests and changelog entry.

deploy-bot: canary build scheduled: redwood-sdk@0.9.3-canary.5 will be available in ~30m in staging. :rocket:

alex_support: told customer about workaround + ask them to try undici patch. they prefer patch from us. i'll follow up after they test staging canary. thanks all :thumbsup:

maria_eng: one more note — document this in SDK troubleshooting doc: "AbortController + retries" with example code and link to canary. prevents repeated support tickets.

tom_runtime: assigning to myself for the PR and QA: i'll post PR link here when created.

alex_support: will update thread with customer repro results.

sophie_sre: ping if they still see fast aborts after canary, we'll rerun load tests.

alex_support: closing the loop later, thx.
